            <ArticleTitle>Rare complication after cardiac surgery: a case report of pyoderma gangrenosum.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>93-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8191.2008.00728.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pyoderma gangrenosum is an uncommon, idiopathic, chronic ulcerative inflammatory skin disease characterized by a rapidly progressive necrosis of the wound edges, and mimics a postoperative infection. Few cases have been reported after cardiothoracic surgery. We present a case of a pyoderma gangrenosum occurring after coronary artery bypass graft.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
